1
00:00:01,935 --> 00:00:03,301
GORDON: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,370 --> 00:00:05,669
- The Doc? You know him?
- I know the Doc.

3
00:00:05,772 --> 00:00:08,799
LEE: <i>Sometimes we search
for things we don't wish to find.</i>

4
00:00:08,876 --> 00:00:10,236
I enjoy being the
queen of Gotham.

5
00:00:10,310 --> 00:00:11,539
Glad we understand each other.

6
00:00:11,645 --> 00:00:13,807
There are other ways
for me to hurt you.

7
00:00:14,348 --> 00:00:15,792
HARVEY: Something's
eating at you, Jim.

8
00:00:15,816 --> 00:00:18,296
And you're not gonna feel
clean till you get it off your chest.

9
00:00:19,253 --> 00:00:20,687
That's done now.

10
00:00:20,888 --> 00:00:23,585
I'm at Sofia Falcone's. I
just shot and killed the Pyg.

11
00:00:24,024 --> 00:00:25,720
<i>I see Arkham's
treating you well.</i>

12
00:00:25,826 --> 00:00:27,226
Goodbye, Oswald.

13
00:00:27,594 --> 00:00:30,154
PENGUIN: <i>"I am held captive.
All my brilliance locked away."</i>

14
00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:31,630
<i>- You're still there.</i>
- (LAUGHING)

15
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:33,176
<i>And you're gonna help
me find a way out of here.</i>

16
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:34,200
I need a name.

17
00:00:34,301 --> 00:00:35,360
- Ivy Pepper.
- I know Ivy.

18
00:00:35,469 --> 00:00:38,234
SELINA: <i>No, Gordon,
she's changed. Like a lot.</i>

19
00:00:38,338 --> 00:00:39,465
Called Lazarus Water.

20
00:00:39,907 --> 00:00:41,384
LUCIUS: <i>What are
you going to do with it?</i>

21
00:00:41,408 --> 00:00:43,206
IVY: <i>I'm going to
make miracles happen.</i>

22
00:00:44,545 --> 00:00:47,014
You'll reel it in a little, or
should I call your keeper?

23
00:00:47,281 --> 00:00:48,881
- Alfred? He won't answer.
- SELINA: <i>Why?</i>

24
00:00:48,949 --> 00:00:50,042
BRUCE: <i>'Cause I fired him.</i>

25
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:48,220
Where's the other
guy who works here?

26
00:01:48,308 --> 00:01:49,401
You mean, Harvey?

27
00:01:49,476 --> 00:01:52,002
He's out sick. You
wanna leave a message?

28
00:01:52,613 --> 00:01:54,172
(CHOMPING)

29
00:01:55,449 --> 00:01:57,145
(SMACKING)

30
00:01:58,151 --> 00:02:00,313
- I do.
- (BURPS)

31
00:02:00,420 --> 00:02:01,649
All right.

32
00:02:01,822 --> 00:02:03,017
What should I say?

33
00:02:03,757 --> 00:02:04,781
Nothing.

34
00:02:05,926 --> 00:02:07,417
Because all of you,

35
00:02:07,894 --> 00:02:11,092
with your blood and your flesh,

36
00:02:12,065 --> 00:02:13,658
and what you will become...

37
00:02:15,936 --> 00:02:17,461
You are the message.

38
00:02:38,091 --> 00:02:39,091
He was a good man.

39
00:02:40,627 --> 00:02:43,426
Doesn't matter that Mario's
gone, you'll always be my sister.

40
00:02:44,431 --> 00:02:46,491
For Falcones, it's
all about family.

41
00:02:47,034 --> 00:02:48,093
I appreciate that.

42
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:51,229
So, sister to sister...

43
00:02:51,972 --> 00:02:54,168
We're not really here
to look at photographs.

44
00:02:57,244 --> 00:03:00,237
There's only one neighborhood in
Gotham that hasn't bent the knee.

45
00:03:00,647 --> 00:03:02,878
The Narrows has never
submitted to an outside boss.

46
00:03:03,183 --> 00:03:05,652
There's never been someone
like me ruling Gotham.

47
00:03:06,486 --> 00:03:07,486
Okay.

48
00:03:07,888 --> 00:03:09,049
What do you want?

49
00:03:09,289 --> 00:03:10,289
A tax.

50
00:03:10,957 --> 00:03:14,826
Thirty percent on all income coming
from The Narrows, legal and illegal.

51
00:03:15,962 --> 00:03:18,727
Every family there lives
hand to mouth. They'll starve.

52
00:03:19,166 --> 00:03:21,067
We all have to make sacrifices.

53
00:03:22,002 --> 00:03:24,233
I'll need an answer
by the end of the day.

54
00:03:29,076 --> 00:03:31,011
You want me to
kiss the ring? I'll do it.

55
00:03:31,244 --> 00:03:34,112
To keep the peace. But what
you're asking for is impossible.

56
00:03:35,782 --> 00:03:37,148
You'll find a way.

57
00:03:39,186 --> 00:03:40,677
Thought it was all about family.

58
00:03:42,923 --> 00:03:44,687
Never said it was
a happy family.

59
00:03:52,532 --> 00:03:53,532
(DOOR OPENS)

60
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:54,727
Thank you.

61
00:04:09,282 --> 00:04:10,841
Thank you for meeting me.

62
00:04:15,722 --> 00:04:18,000
My parents' foundation is
having their annual dinner tonight.

63
00:04:18,024 --> 00:04:19,185
I thought we could go.

64
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:20,937
Somehow, I don't think you
got me all the way down here

65
00:04:20,961 --> 00:04:22,930
to talk about a
fundraiser, did you?

66
00:04:25,332 --> 00:04:28,769
Bruce, what exactly is it
that you want from me?

67
00:04:35,108 --> 00:04:36,167
Help.

68
00:04:37,744 --> 00:04:40,304
Figuring this out. I
can't do it alone, I...

69
00:04:42,449 --> 00:04:44,077
Alfred, I need your help.

70
00:04:49,556 --> 00:04:50,556
No.

71
00:04:53,927 --> 00:04:54,927
What?

72
00:04:54,995 --> 00:04:58,090
Listen, you can't just waltz
back in here and expect me to go

73
00:04:58,165 --> 00:05:00,930
and clean your smalls and cook
your tea. After what you've done.

74
00:05:01,001 --> 00:05:02,936
Alfred, I'm not asking
for that. I've changed.

75
00:05:03,003 --> 00:05:04,027
You have, have you?

76
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:06,368
It's one thing saying
that you've changed,

77
00:05:06,473 --> 00:05:08,271
and another actually changing.

78
00:05:09,209 --> 00:05:14,079
So show me. Show me how you've
changed, and I might reconsider.

79
00:05:17,350 --> 00:05:18,443
Show you how?

80
00:05:25,592 --> 00:05:27,220
That's for you to
figure out, innit?

81
00:05:33,233 --> 00:05:35,998
I'm asking as a friend.

82
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:38,331
I'm not your friend.

83
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:41,803
I was your butler.

84
00:05:43,643 --> 00:05:44,838
And you fired me.

85
00:05:49,983 --> 00:05:51,315
He'll pay for the tea, miss.

86
00:06:02,395 --> 00:06:04,830
Sure hope Lee is gonna
figure something out with Sofia.

87
00:06:05,098 --> 00:06:06,691
Lee being the love
of your life and all.

88
00:06:07,534 --> 00:06:08,729
We're friends.

89
00:06:09,436 --> 00:06:11,871
You know, those koo-koo pills
aren't gonna make me go away.

90
00:06:13,306 --> 00:06:15,639
Well, they have stopped
you from getting out

91
00:06:15,709 --> 00:06:18,474
and trying to kill Lee
again. So works for me.

92
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:21,546
Mail arrived.

93
00:06:25,418 --> 00:06:26,818
Oh, who's it from?

94
00:06:27,587 --> 00:06:28,714
Oswald.

95
00:06:29,055 --> 00:06:32,787
"I want to apologize...
Can we be friends again?"

96
00:06:32,893 --> 00:06:35,522
What? I'm never
gonna forgive him.

97
00:06:35,595 --> 00:06:37,564
I think it's a nice letter.

98
00:06:37,631 --> 00:06:39,896
- Shut up!
- Hey, Ed.

99
00:06:40,533 --> 00:06:42,263
What has two eyes but can't see?

100
00:06:43,103 --> 00:06:44,332
What has two...

101
00:06:44,437 --> 00:06:46,065
(LAUGHING)

102
00:06:54,547 --> 00:06:56,175
Good lord.

103
00:06:56,583 --> 00:06:58,950
This is new. More aggressive.

104
00:07:00,587 --> 00:07:02,707
The plants are literally
bursting through their flesh.

105
00:07:02,756 --> 00:07:04,247
(INDISTINCT RADIO CHATTER)

106
00:07:05,325 --> 00:07:08,124
You! Get away from that! Now!

107
00:07:08,228 --> 00:07:09,321
Now.

108
00:07:09,930 --> 00:07:12,229
Same flower growing
out of these bodies.

109
00:07:13,066 --> 00:07:14,329
That's a weapon?

110
00:07:15,435 --> 00:07:18,303
Gordon, this must be what
Ivy did with the Lazarus Water.

111
00:07:18,405 --> 00:07:20,772
Used it to increase the
potency of a toxic plant.

112
00:07:20,874 --> 00:07:22,852
- The seeds made it airborne...
- GORDON: Where's Bullock?

113
00:07:22,876 --> 00:07:24,708
- What?
- He works here.

114
00:07:25,879 --> 00:07:27,438
Harvey killed Ivy's father.

115
00:07:36,957 --> 00:07:37,981
Too late.

116
00:07:38,291 --> 00:07:39,452
No, we're not.

117
00:07:39,859 --> 00:07:40,859
Hey.

118
00:07:41,361 --> 00:07:42,454
Hey!

119
00:07:43,697 --> 00:07:45,165
Damn it, Jim!

120
00:07:45,632 --> 00:07:46,930
Jim, what the hell?

121
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:49,235
Hey, someone's
paying for that door!

122
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:50,326
Ivy Pepper.

123
00:07:51,171 --> 00:07:52,764
- Who?
- Mario Pepper's kid.

124
00:07:52,839 --> 00:07:54,569
She's been working
on some biotech.

125
00:07:55,008 --> 00:07:56,408
She attacked your bar.

126
00:07:57,010 --> 00:07:58,010
It's bad.

127
00:07:58,812 --> 00:08:00,178
Donnie, the bartender...

128
00:08:01,781 --> 00:08:02,942
I'm sorry.

129
00:08:03,350 --> 00:08:04,350
Oh, God!

130
00:08:04,851 --> 00:08:08,151
Look, I gotta think
that you were the target.

131
00:08:08,621 --> 00:08:12,717
Jim, I only shot Ivy Pepper's dad
because I was saving your stupid eye.

132
00:08:13,193 --> 00:08:14,491
You can't put this on me.

133
00:08:14,594 --> 00:08:16,620
- I'm not putting it on you.
- ALVAREZ: Guys.

134
00:08:17,664 --> 00:08:19,428
<i>We have decided
to share the footage.</i>

135
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:21,593
<i>So in a moment the video
we are about to show you</i>

136
00:08:21,668 --> 00:08:23,967
<i>is from a tape
received this morning.</i>

137
00:08:24,537 --> 00:08:26,028
<i>And again, let me warn you.</i>

138
00:08:26,439 --> 00:08:28,203
<i>It is very disturbing.</i>

139
00:08:30,043 --> 00:08:31,534
<i>Plants love us.</i>

140
00:08:32,345 --> 00:08:37,682
<i>They give us food, shelter,
the very air we breathe.</i>

141
00:08:38,918 --> 00:08:40,511
<i>But what do we do in return?</i>

142
00:08:41,988 --> 00:08:45,356
<i>Kill them. Because
that's our nature.</i>

143
00:08:47,394 --> 00:08:49,659
<i>We cause pain.</i>

144
00:08:51,998 --> 00:08:57,062
<i>Everyone I've known has
only hurt or betrayed me.</i>

145
00:08:58,071 --> 00:09:01,337
<i>Maybe I've always known in
my heart what I needed to do.</i>

146
00:09:01,875 --> 00:09:04,868
<i>But I finally have
the power to do so.</i>

147
00:09:06,513 --> 00:09:09,506
<i>I'm giving your city
back to the plants.</i>

148
00:09:10,016 --> 00:09:11,712
<i>Starting with the
people who hurt me.</i>

149
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:17,213
<i>So if that's you,
your time is coming.</i>

150
00:09:19,859 --> 00:09:22,021
- Guess we know what she's up to.
- Yeah.

151
00:09:22,095 --> 00:09:24,030
She's gonna kill
everyone in Gotham.

152
00:09:24,864 --> 00:09:26,332
Starting with me.

153
00:09:30,570 --> 00:09:34,439
WOMAN: <i>Preliminary reports indicate
that similar tapes have been delivered</i>

154
00:09:34,541 --> 00:09:36,373
<i>to multiple news organizations.</i>

155
00:09:37,377 --> 00:09:38,377
Wait a minute.

156
00:09:39,212 --> 00:09:40,212
What's that there?

157
00:09:41,381 --> 00:09:42,644
HARVEY: Sully's Eatery.

158
00:09:43,149 --> 00:09:45,709
That's in Ives Square.
House must be right across.

159
00:09:46,152 --> 00:09:47,415
You should go to the precinct.

160
00:09:47,487 --> 00:09:49,979
Hey, I'm not hiding like some
freaking coward. All right?

161
00:09:50,090 --> 00:09:52,321
Four people are dead
because she wanted me.

162
00:09:52,659 --> 00:09:55,754
Okay, then we'll work on it
together. You can wear the badge.

163
00:09:55,829 --> 00:09:58,822
Get this straight, Jim. I ain't
working for you now or ever.

164
00:09:59,499 --> 00:10:01,627
I got more contacts in The
Narrows than any of you.

165
00:10:02,435 --> 00:10:04,495
I'm gonna find her. Alone.

166
00:10:09,209 --> 00:10:10,973
Once I find my pants.

167
00:10:15,949 --> 00:10:17,212
LEE: Doesn't make any sense.

168
00:10:19,452 --> 00:10:20,784
There's no money here.

169
00:10:20,987 --> 00:10:22,421
Okay, so it's about power.

170
00:10:24,324 --> 00:10:25,656
I offered to bend the knee.

171
00:10:28,394 --> 00:10:31,262
She's asking for something
she knew I couldn't give.

172
00:10:32,665 --> 00:10:33,758
She wants...

173
00:10:35,401 --> 00:10:37,131
She wants to punish me.

174
00:10:37,770 --> 00:10:39,170
For what?

175
00:10:39,372 --> 00:10:42,001
I don't know. But you
can't fight an enemy

176
00:10:42,108 --> 00:10:44,509
whose motivations you
don't understand, Lee.

177
00:10:50,350 --> 00:10:54,481
You are the greatest
spies in all of Gotham.

178
00:10:55,455 --> 00:10:57,447
You have eyes and
ears everywhere.

179
00:10:58,725 --> 00:11:03,186
The survival of The
Narrows depends upon you.

180
00:11:06,132 --> 00:11:09,500
Whoever learns why Sofia Falcone
wants to destroy Lee Thompkins

181
00:11:09,602 --> 00:11:13,596
will receive a complete
set of encyclopedias.

182
00:11:14,107 --> 00:11:15,268
Minus the T.

183
00:11:19,312 --> 00:11:20,336
Plus 20 bucks.

184
00:11:20,446 --> 00:11:22,142
- Yes!
- Yeah!

185
00:11:22,315 --> 00:11:23,339
Go get 'em.

186
00:11:27,954 --> 00:11:30,321
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

187
00:11:31,291 --> 00:11:32,850
OFFICER: We're moving, clear.

188
00:11:35,962 --> 00:11:37,294
She wasn't bluffing.

189
00:11:37,697 --> 00:11:40,667
With this many plants, she could kill
hundreds if not thousands of people.

190
00:11:42,068 --> 00:11:44,388
Search the other room for any
signs of where she's heading.

191
00:11:54,948 --> 00:11:56,211
What are you gonna do to her?

192
00:11:58,051 --> 00:12:00,282
- Where is she?
- I don't know.

193
00:12:01,754 --> 00:12:03,086
I just saw the news.

194
00:12:03,690 --> 00:12:05,283
She killed four
more people today.

195
00:12:05,959 --> 00:12:08,451
You knew where she was
staying. If you had told me,

196
00:12:08,761 --> 00:12:10,753
- we could've saved lives.
- Or not.

197
00:12:11,598 --> 00:12:14,659
I mean, you couldn't even stop
her from hypnotizing your own cops.

198
00:12:16,002 --> 00:12:17,334
So why did you come here?

199
00:12:19,939 --> 00:12:21,373
To try to reason with her.

200
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:23,770
Have you heard a word
she said? She's a fanatic.

201
00:12:23,876 --> 00:12:24,876
She's my friend.

202
00:12:25,878 --> 00:12:27,176
What do you expect me to do?

203
00:12:27,947 --> 00:12:30,075
She contacts you again, call me.

204
00:12:30,917 --> 00:12:33,113
I'll try and find her,
and bring her in quietly.

205
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:35,384
Otherwise, stay out of her way.

206
00:12:38,458 --> 00:12:39,687
Harvey?

207
00:12:40,226 --> 00:12:42,491
Hey, I got a lead.

208
00:12:43,263 --> 00:12:44,287
Great.

209
00:12:48,234 --> 00:12:49,394
HARVEY: I knocked some heads.

210
00:12:49,435 --> 00:12:52,837
Heard a hot redhead was poking
around in that dive bar next door.

211
00:12:52,939 --> 00:12:55,135
That is the place in The
Narrows for low-end muscle.

212
00:12:55,241 --> 00:12:57,176
So I figured, if she was
planning something big,

213
00:12:57,277 --> 00:12:58,768
she might've gone
there to recruit.

214
00:12:59,345 --> 00:13:00,472
That's the back entrance.

215
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:02,020
That's where my
contact said that...

216
00:13:02,115 --> 00:13:03,139
(DOOR OPENS)

217
00:13:06,185 --> 00:13:07,653
Hello, Detective Gordon.

218
00:13:07,754 --> 00:13:10,189
On the ground.
Now. Harvey, call it in.

219
00:13:11,924 --> 00:13:13,893
She's beautiful,
don't you think, Jim?

220
00:13:15,995 --> 00:13:17,429
Drop your weapon.

221
00:13:23,136 --> 00:13:24,297
(WHISTLES)

222
00:13:24,637 --> 00:13:25,969
You don't look good.

223
00:13:26,606 --> 00:13:28,766
I think you might be exceeding
your recommended dosage.

224
00:13:28,941 --> 00:13:32,343
Are you experiencing
"trembling extremities"?

225
00:13:33,313 --> 00:13:36,579
Check. "Cognitive
impairment"? Definite check.

226
00:13:36,649 --> 00:13:39,312
Though to be fair,
how would you know?

227
00:13:39,852 --> 00:13:41,013
Shut up!

228
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:43,680
Take all the pills you want,
Ed. I'm only getting stronger.

229
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:47,791
Soon I'm gonna be
out, and the fun begins.

230
00:13:47,860 --> 00:13:50,989
No. I won't let you. 'Cause
I know what you'll do.

231
00:13:51,064 --> 00:13:52,965
Oh, you mean kill Lee?

232
00:13:53,466 --> 00:13:56,903
Yeah, I guess I will do
that. And you can't stop me.

233
00:13:57,003 --> 00:13:58,562
There are things that I can do.

234
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:00,970
Like what? You
need to face it, pal.

235
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:03,339
The only way you'll get
rid of me is to kill yourself.

236
00:14:07,213 --> 00:14:09,079
I guess you are smarter than me.

237
00:14:11,584 --> 00:14:13,348
- You wouldn't actually...
- Oh, yeah.

238
00:14:16,556 --> 00:14:17,956
Oh, yeah.

239
00:14:19,325 --> 00:14:21,317
I said drop the gun, Jim.

240
00:14:28,735 --> 00:14:31,330
Do you believe in
fate, Detective Gordon?

241
00:14:32,038 --> 00:14:35,975
I went out today to test my plants
on the man who shot my father.

242
00:14:37,410 --> 00:14:40,710
He wasn't there.
That's disappointing.

243
00:14:42,248 --> 00:14:43,910
Then he found me.

244
00:14:45,351 --> 00:14:49,288
And I realized I could make
him deliver his partner as well.

245
00:14:51,023 --> 00:14:52,252
Fate.

246
00:14:52,358 --> 00:14:54,384
Stay strong, Harvey.
She's controlling you.

247
00:14:54,460 --> 00:14:55,758
I kinda like it, Jim.

248
00:14:56,596 --> 00:14:57,757
Sweet surrender.

249
00:14:58,631 --> 00:15:00,259
GORDON: You need help, Ivy.

250
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:02,626
Let me find Selina.
She wants to help.

251
00:15:02,735 --> 00:15:03,735
Quiet.

252
00:15:04,737 --> 00:15:06,035
I have to go.

253
00:15:06,472 --> 00:15:08,464
Big plans tonight.
Lots of people to kill.

254
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:11,237
- Detective Bullock?
- Ma'am.

255
00:15:11,310 --> 00:15:15,213
After you kill your partner, be sure
to shoot yourself in the head, okay?

256
00:15:15,281 --> 00:15:16,281
Copy that.

257
00:15:17,417 --> 00:15:19,045
(IVY HUMMING)

258
00:15:21,954 --> 00:15:23,217
(DOOR CLOSES)

259
00:15:24,357 --> 00:15:25,357
Harvey...

260
00:15:25,425 --> 00:15:27,102
Don't even try and
talk your way out of this.

261
00:15:27,126 --> 00:15:30,187
I wouldn't. But, quick question.

262
00:15:31,531 --> 00:15:33,966
Is Ivy's hair more
auburn or scarlet?

263
00:15:35,301 --> 00:15:36,633
I, uh...

264
00:15:37,069 --> 00:15:38,469
That's a good...

265
00:15:38,571 --> 00:15:40,540
(GUNSHOTS)

266
00:15:40,606 --> 00:15:41,699
(GUN CLICKING)

267
00:15:44,777 --> 00:15:46,871
You think I didn't
come prepared, huh?

268
00:15:48,748 --> 00:15:50,740
You always underestimate me.

269
00:15:52,452 --> 00:15:54,080
That's not why I'm shooting you.

270
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:57,613
I just think we should,
uh, clear the air.

271
00:15:59,091 --> 00:16:01,083
What do you wanna
talk about? I'm all ears.

272
00:16:02,995 --> 00:16:05,191
How you stole
my job for starters.

273
00:16:06,599 --> 00:16:08,625
GORDON: Was it
really your job, though?

274
00:16:09,035 --> 00:16:11,834
I mean, you only got it
'cause one captain died

275
00:16:11,938 --> 00:16:13,304
and the other one went nuts.

276
00:16:13,372 --> 00:16:14,465
Like hell!

277
00:16:14,941 --> 00:16:17,706
I paid my dues! I earned
that job, and you took it!

278
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:20,439
You mean like the time
you gut-shot Officer Patel?

279
00:16:21,814 --> 00:16:24,511
That was a mistake.

280
00:16:24,750 --> 00:16:27,015
GORDON: Hey, give
yourself some credit.

281
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:29,184
You did shoot her
from across the room.

282
00:16:29,522 --> 00:16:31,821
Although you couldn't
face her later, remember?

283
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:35,659
You didn't have the courage to
meet her the next day, did you?

284
00:16:37,163 --> 00:16:38,961
- You coward.
- Screw you!

285
00:16:39,031 --> 00:16:41,000
(GUNSHOTS)

286
00:17:02,822 --> 00:17:04,688
- We're not open.
- I wanted to see you.

287
00:17:04,757 --> 00:17:07,818
Why? Because you weren't big
enough of an ass the last time I saw you?

288
00:17:08,394 --> 00:17:10,693
- Selina...
- I don't have time for this, Bruce.

289
00:17:11,731 --> 00:17:12,858
Something happened.

290
00:17:13,499 --> 00:17:16,025
- I need to talk to someone.
- Okay, then go find Alfred.

291
00:17:18,404 --> 00:17:19,929
Oh...

292
00:17:20,339 --> 00:17:23,901
You did, and he wanted
nothing to do with you.

293
00:17:25,411 --> 00:17:27,073
Smart guy, Alfred.

294
00:17:29,148 --> 00:17:30,859
- Can you at least hear me out?
- No, Bruce.

295
00:17:30,883 --> 00:17:32,408
Because Ivy's out
there killing people

296
00:17:32,518 --> 00:17:33,986
and I need to find
her and stop her.

297
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:36,648
So whatever problem you
have going on right now,

298
00:17:36,722 --> 00:17:38,156
you need to figure it out.

299
00:17:38,591 --> 00:17:40,389
I mean, say sorry to Alfred.

300
00:17:41,661 --> 00:17:44,153
'Cause I'm sure whatever
happened was your fault.

301
00:17:52,405 --> 00:17:54,067
According to my spies,

302
00:17:55,241 --> 00:17:58,643
Sofia and Jim were
carrying out an affair

303
00:17:59,946 --> 00:18:01,141
till Jim ended it.

304
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:03,276
So, technically,

305
00:18:03,583 --> 00:18:06,985
your ex has been sleeping with
your dead husband's mafiosa sister...

306
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:08,452
Okay, I get it.

307
00:18:11,490 --> 00:18:14,050
If Sofia was sleeping with
the captain of the GCPD,

308
00:18:14,126 --> 00:18:16,891
it was a power
play. And it failed.

309
00:18:18,064 --> 00:18:19,589
I'm her next step.

310
00:18:21,734 --> 00:18:23,726
Why don't I just give
her what she wants?

311
00:18:24,403 --> 00:18:26,235
Power over Jim Gordon.

312
00:18:27,974 --> 00:18:29,306
You would do that?

313
00:18:30,076 --> 00:18:32,477
I'm not trying to get back at
Jim, though he deserves it.

314
00:18:33,412 --> 00:18:36,746
My job is to make sure that the
people of The Narrows are safe.

315
00:18:36,816 --> 00:18:39,547
And I will do everything
in my power to ensure that.

316
00:18:44,991 --> 00:18:46,289
What?

317
00:18:47,093 --> 00:18:48,755
Lee, I...

318
00:18:58,270 --> 00:18:59,761
I have to leave.

319
00:19:12,451 --> 00:19:15,285
- Harvey. Harvey, come on, buddy.
- Where am I?

320
00:19:15,988 --> 00:19:18,480
You were hypnotized.
I need you to focus.

321
00:19:18,724 --> 00:19:21,284
Did Ivy give you any clue
about who she's targeting next?

322
00:19:21,394 --> 00:19:23,022
I can't believe I
let her get to me.

323
00:19:23,129 --> 00:19:25,860
Hey, you wanna help? Here's
how. Did she say anything?

324
00:19:27,533 --> 00:19:31,129
Something about, "They
get rich by murdering plants."

325
00:19:32,004 --> 00:19:33,836
So she's targeting a
group of rich people.

326
00:19:35,541 --> 00:19:39,501
At her place, she was trying
on fancy clothes, fancy shoes.

327
00:19:40,012 --> 00:19:41,036
A party?

328
00:19:41,147 --> 00:19:43,378
She said she had big
plans, couldn't be late.

329
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:46,952
- Yeah, black tie.
- No, no, no, come on.

330
00:19:47,019 --> 00:19:49,147
Fancy schmancy, like a
charity for hobos or something.

331
00:19:49,221 --> 00:19:51,713
Wayne Foundation's
annual dinner is tonight

332
00:19:51,857 --> 00:19:53,120
over at Gotham Square.

333
00:19:53,325 --> 00:19:54,816
All right. Get the strike force.

334
00:19:54,894 --> 00:19:57,557
I want full body armor, gas
masks, nonlethal rounds.

335
00:19:58,698 --> 00:19:59,825
To fight plants?

336
00:19:59,932 --> 00:20:03,425
When Ivy got me, she was
hypnotizing a bunch of low-end muscle.

337
00:20:03,602 --> 00:20:04,602
Go.

338
00:20:09,442 --> 00:20:10,882
We could really
use you there, Harv.

339
00:20:11,711 --> 00:20:13,407
Jim, she got in my head.

340
00:20:14,380 --> 00:20:16,611
I really... I just don't
trust myself right now.

341
00:20:16,782 --> 00:20:19,718
All right, you can help
out here. Man the phones.

342
00:20:24,857 --> 00:20:25,950
Hey, Jim.

343
00:20:28,527 --> 00:20:30,496
I spent too long
putting this all on you.

344
00:20:31,931 --> 00:20:33,365
What happened between us.

345
00:20:35,768 --> 00:20:38,203
The fact is I only
got myself to blame.

346
00:20:42,842 --> 00:20:43,935
I'll call.

347
00:20:48,714 --> 00:20:50,580
(CLASSICAL MUSIC PLAYING)

348
00:20:53,018 --> 00:20:54,748
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

349
00:21:06,732 --> 00:21:08,428
And now, ladies and gentleman,

350
00:21:08,601 --> 00:21:13,665
please welcome to the
stage our host Bruce Wayne.

351
00:21:14,406 --> 00:21:16,136
(APPLAUSE)

352
00:21:26,819 --> 00:21:28,014
Good evening.

353
00:21:29,488 --> 00:21:31,184
Welcome to the
third annual dinner

354
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:33,885
for the Thomas and
Martha Wayne Foundation.

355
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:37,327
This year we
disbursed $4 million...

356
00:21:43,335 --> 00:21:44,894
Um...

357
00:21:46,305 --> 00:21:51,334
We disbursed $4
million and, uh...

358
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:08,817
My parents spent their
lives helping people.

359
00:22:12,031 --> 00:22:15,524
I was so proud of them, and I
always wanted them to be proud of me.

360
00:22:21,173 --> 00:22:22,869
And then I saw
them get murdered.

361
00:22:25,544 --> 00:22:28,070
I survived because someone
in my life kept me going.

362
00:22:30,649 --> 00:22:32,413
He's been everything to me.

363
00:22:34,553 --> 00:22:35,714
A teacher,

364
00:22:36,689 --> 00:22:37,850
a protector.

365
00:22:41,293 --> 00:22:42,659
He's been a father to me.

366
00:22:46,365 --> 00:22:47,560
I hope...

367
00:22:48,734 --> 00:22:50,202
I hope he can see that.

368
00:22:53,639 --> 00:22:55,005
And give me another chance.

369
00:22:58,811 --> 00:22:59,972
Thank you.

370
00:23:01,714 --> 00:23:03,239
(APPLAUDING)

371
00:23:12,224 --> 00:23:13,522
Thank you.

372
00:23:15,294 --> 00:23:16,762
That meant a great deal.

373
00:23:18,631 --> 00:23:20,122
But I can't help you.

374
00:23:22,101 --> 00:23:25,265
Not until you accept
who you really are.

375
00:23:27,606 --> 00:23:29,939
I know who I am, I've
seen what's inside of me.

376
00:23:30,109 --> 00:23:32,078
Darkness and anger?

377
00:23:32,711 --> 00:23:34,111
But what's beneath that?

378
00:23:35,381 --> 00:23:37,509
It's a heart that feels pain.

379
00:23:37,583 --> 00:23:40,849
Your heart is what makes
you want to help other people.

380
00:23:41,053 --> 00:23:42,919
Your heart is your strength.

381
00:23:45,090 --> 00:23:47,753
Deny the darkness
and you deny that.

382
00:23:49,295 --> 00:23:52,129
But accepting that is something
that you must do on your own.

383
00:23:52,231 --> 00:23:53,699
Do you understand me?

384
00:23:57,770 --> 00:23:59,568
I was stupid for reaching out.

385
00:24:05,744 --> 00:24:07,235
WOMAN: That was quite a speech.

386
00:24:07,746 --> 00:24:08,975
Hello all.

387
00:24:11,150 --> 00:24:12,277
I'm Ivy Pepper.

388
00:24:12,685 --> 00:24:15,177
- (CROWD GASPS)
- No, no, no, please.

389
00:24:16,121 --> 00:24:17,248
Stay seated.

390
00:24:20,192 --> 00:24:21,660
(WOMEN SCREAMING)

391
00:24:34,306 --> 00:24:35,330
RIDDLER: <i>Can I just say?</i>

392
00:24:36,308 --> 00:24:37,640
This is crazy!

393
00:24:39,311 --> 00:24:40,939
Well, this whole thing

394
00:24:41,013 --> 00:24:42,345
was your idea.

395
00:24:43,415 --> 00:24:45,975
And you're the smart
one, as you always tell me.

396
00:24:46,085 --> 00:24:47,348
Very funny.

397
00:24:48,821 --> 00:24:50,813
Okay, fine! Fine!

398
00:24:51,190 --> 00:24:52,419
You win!

399
00:24:53,258 --> 00:24:55,921
- What?
- You win.

400
00:24:56,929 --> 00:24:59,694
You beat me. Is that
what you wanna hear?

401
00:25:00,432 --> 00:25:01,866
That is very nice.

402
00:25:03,168 --> 00:25:04,864
But I still have to do it.

403
00:25:05,504 --> 00:25:07,496
Wait! Wait!

404
00:25:07,840 --> 00:25:09,706
Wait! What if there's a way

405
00:25:09,875 --> 00:25:11,707
to do this where
nobody gets hurt?

406
00:25:13,045 --> 00:25:14,206
I don't believe you.

407
00:25:14,313 --> 00:25:16,713
So you're just going to kill
yourself without hearing me out?

408
00:25:18,751 --> 00:25:20,014
I'm telling you, Ed.

409
00:25:20,085 --> 00:25:23,078
There is a way to save
Lee without killing yourself.

410
00:25:25,357 --> 00:25:26,552
Or killing us.

411
00:25:31,030 --> 00:25:32,089
I'm listening.

412
00:25:36,001 --> 00:25:39,096
Aren't these crimson
flowers lovely?

413
00:25:45,644 --> 00:25:47,010
You're a handsome man.

414
00:25:48,480 --> 00:25:50,381
But you want more from life.

415
00:25:51,016 --> 00:25:52,016
I can feel it.

416
00:25:58,157 --> 00:25:59,420
(CHOKING)

417
00:26:01,060 --> 00:26:03,256
Bruce, is Ivy Pepper in there?

418
00:26:03,362 --> 00:26:04,421
BRUCE: Ivy?

419
00:26:04,530 --> 00:26:06,089
No, I didn't see her.

420
00:26:06,198 --> 00:26:07,496
(WOMEN SCREAMING)

421
00:26:07,566 --> 00:26:08,727
Get out of here.

422
00:26:08,834 --> 00:26:09,995
Let's go!

423
00:26:11,937 --> 00:26:13,371
GORDON: Breach that door.

424
00:26:24,750 --> 00:26:25,911
We

425
00:26:26,318 --> 00:26:28,378
Are going to turn this room

426
00:26:29,054 --> 00:26:32,786
into the most gorgeous
garden the world has ever seen.

427
00:26:34,593 --> 00:26:36,255
All you have to do

428
00:26:37,229 --> 00:26:39,892
is take a deep breath.

429
00:26:42,768 --> 00:26:43,895
Oh,

430
00:26:44,603 --> 00:26:45,935
a volunteer.

431
00:26:46,472 --> 00:26:48,407
- (CURTAINS RUSTLING)
- (GRUNTS)

432
00:26:48,474 --> 00:26:49,874
GCPD!

433
00:26:49,942 --> 00:26:51,376
GCPD!

434
00:26:52,311 --> 00:26:54,371
Drop your guns.
On the ground, now!

435
00:26:56,882 --> 00:26:58,077
Kill everyone.

436
00:26:59,051 --> 00:27:00,815
- (GUNSHOTS)
- (SCREAMING)

437
00:27:09,828 --> 00:27:11,558
You got this, I'm
going after Ivy.

438
00:27:37,689 --> 00:27:39,658
(ELECTRICAL BUZZING)

439
00:27:44,463 --> 00:27:45,624
(GRUNTING)

440
00:27:50,202 --> 00:27:51,746
I'm getting you out of
here. Come on, let's go.

441
00:27:51,770 --> 00:27:53,363
Listen, listen.

442
00:27:53,972 --> 00:27:55,338
People need your help.

443
00:27:56,608 --> 00:27:58,668
This is who you are.

444
00:28:16,695 --> 00:28:18,535
MAN: Watch the door.
I'm gonna go look for him.

445
00:28:18,864 --> 00:28:21,595
Where'd you go, punk? You
can run, but you can't hide.

446
00:28:24,937 --> 00:28:26,337
(GRUNTING)

447
00:28:31,843 --> 00:28:33,539
GORDON: Hey! Hey!

448
00:28:34,046 --> 00:28:35,378
- Drop it!
- No!

449
00:28:41,853 --> 00:28:43,185
(GASPING)

450
00:28:46,391 --> 00:28:47,791
Hey. Hey.

451
00:29:05,877 --> 00:29:07,743
(SIREN WAILING)

452
00:29:16,722 --> 00:29:18,384
(HELICOPTER HOVERING)

453
00:29:41,513 --> 00:29:42,845
SELINA: You hear the news?

454
00:29:43,615 --> 00:29:47,177
"Crazy Ivy Pepper attacks
the Wayne Foundation dinner."

455
00:29:49,521 --> 00:29:52,582
I'll be honest. The evening didn't
turn out quite the way I'd hoped.

456
00:29:52,924 --> 00:29:53,948
(SCOFFS)

457
00:29:54,092 --> 00:29:56,391
You mean you didn't get
to kill everyone in there?

458
00:29:57,262 --> 00:29:58,560
Something like that.

459
00:29:59,131 --> 00:30:00,258
You got out.

460
00:30:00,832 --> 00:30:02,095
Made it back here.

461
00:30:05,904 --> 00:30:07,497
You always were the survivor.

462
00:30:09,474 --> 00:30:11,340
No, you taught me that, Selina.

463
00:30:14,079 --> 00:30:15,843
What's in the bag, Ivy?

464
00:30:24,056 --> 00:30:25,854
It's the last of
the Lazarus Water

465
00:30:25,957 --> 00:30:27,323
I stole from Wayne Enterprises.

466
00:30:28,794 --> 00:30:29,955
So you can go

467
00:30:30,028 --> 00:30:32,293
and make more
plants to kill people?

468
00:30:37,336 --> 00:30:38,861
Yeah, that ain't gonna happen.

469
00:30:42,007 --> 00:30:44,067
Are you gonna stop me, Selina?

470
00:30:45,344 --> 00:30:47,506
You're gonna remind me

471
00:30:47,846 --> 00:30:49,041
of the old days?

472
00:30:49,548 --> 00:30:51,540
- Tell me I'm not this person?
- (CHUCKLES)

473
00:30:52,017 --> 00:30:54,885
No, I think we're
past words now.

474
00:31:01,126 --> 00:31:02,321
(GROANS)

475
00:31:04,129 --> 00:31:05,358
Well,

476
00:31:05,464 --> 00:31:06,898
Selina Kyle

477
00:31:07,532 --> 00:31:09,467
turns out to be the hero.

478
00:31:15,140 --> 00:31:16,540
I'm no hero.

479
00:31:18,143 --> 00:31:19,634
(GRUNTING)

480
00:31:23,849 --> 00:31:26,080
One scratch is
all it takes, Selina.

481
00:31:27,085 --> 00:31:29,054
And there's no
antidote this time.

482
00:31:29,921 --> 00:31:32,083
And there's no more
jumping across rooftops

483
00:31:32,190 --> 00:31:34,455
for little dead Selina.

484
00:31:34,960 --> 00:31:36,292
I'll keep that in mind.

485
00:31:42,200 --> 00:31:43,896
You're gonna have
to fight me, Selina.

486
00:31:45,237 --> 00:31:46,762
You can't run forever.

487
00:31:49,274 --> 00:31:50,867
I wasn't running. (PANTING)

488
00:31:51,877 --> 00:31:53,436
I was getting this.

489
00:31:55,580 --> 00:31:58,243
This is what you're gonna use
to make all your little plants?

490
00:31:59,851 --> 00:32:02,844
So, I guess it's safe to
say that I shouldn't drop it.

491
00:32:02,921 --> 00:32:04,389
Stop, Selina.

492
00:32:05,457 --> 00:32:06,857
I will let you leave.

493
00:32:06,925 --> 00:32:08,188
Let me?

494
00:32:08,393 --> 00:32:10,021
(SNORTS)

495
00:32:10,962 --> 00:32:15,127
You're not gonna turn me
into some geranium-type thing?

496
00:32:16,968 --> 00:32:18,869
That's so generous.

497
00:32:20,439 --> 00:32:21,600
No!

498
00:32:26,077 --> 00:32:27,409
How can you side with them?

499
00:32:29,514 --> 00:32:31,483
All the people who hurt us.

500
00:32:35,020 --> 00:32:36,682
You think they're innocent?

501
00:32:38,523 --> 00:32:39,923
They're guilty.

502
00:32:41,259 --> 00:32:43,922
Every person in this city,

503
00:32:44,796 --> 00:32:46,287
they spew out poison.

504
00:32:48,099 --> 00:32:50,159
How are you not choking on it?

505
00:32:51,636 --> 00:32:55,164
The only thing that I'm
choking on, Ivy, is your insanity.

506
00:33:02,247 --> 00:33:03,408
(GRUNTS)

507
00:33:06,284 --> 00:33:07,444
You shouldn't have done that.

508
00:33:09,621 --> 00:33:10,782
Now, you're gonna die.

509
00:33:10,856 --> 00:33:12,256
Ivy, look down.

510
00:33:21,500 --> 00:33:23,366
- Well?
- Yeah.

511
00:33:25,604 --> 00:33:29,302
So, what happens
now? We kill each other?

512
00:33:29,374 --> 00:33:30,569
That's an option.

513
00:33:31,676 --> 00:33:33,838
You always did think
you were better than me.

514
00:33:33,912 --> 00:33:35,813
That's not true. I
was your friend.

515
00:33:36,581 --> 00:33:39,210
We were friends, Ivy.
You said so yourself.

516
00:33:42,420 --> 00:33:44,013
That was a long time ago.

517
00:33:45,357 --> 00:33:46,882
I'm a different person now.

518
00:33:51,396 --> 00:33:53,228
This isn't what I want.

519
00:34:11,149 --> 00:34:12,708
Don't get in my way again.

520
00:34:28,900 --> 00:34:31,131
MAN: Lift your hands
up. Got any weapons?

521
00:34:33,038 --> 00:34:35,974
I'd almost think this wasn't
going to be a friendly conversation.

522
00:34:36,575 --> 00:34:37,804
Just being careful.

523
00:34:37,909 --> 00:34:39,070
- They're clean.
- Okay.

524
00:34:39,945 --> 00:34:41,106
Smart lady.

525
00:34:42,414 --> 00:34:45,748
So, you said you wanted 30%
of everything in The Narrows?

526
00:34:47,085 --> 00:34:49,748
What if I told you I had
something more valuable to offer?

527
00:34:50,956 --> 00:34:52,083
Such as?

528
00:34:53,625 --> 00:34:54,923
Jim Gordon.

529
00:34:57,729 --> 00:35:00,096
I know crimes he's
committed no one else does.

530
00:35:00,832 --> 00:35:02,528
It would give you
control over him.

531
00:35:03,768 --> 00:35:06,260
Surely that's worth
more than 30% of this.

532
00:35:06,438 --> 00:35:08,236
I have my own
dirt on Jim Gordon.

533
00:35:08,473 --> 00:35:09,873
But you can't use it.

534
00:35:11,042 --> 00:35:13,568
Otherwise, you wouldn't be
sitting there threatening me,

535
00:35:14,112 --> 00:35:15,410
would you?

536
00:35:18,750 --> 00:35:19,877
Sofia?

537
00:35:21,620 --> 00:35:23,088
Take my deal.

538
00:35:29,294 --> 00:35:31,490
I have a better way to
bring Gordon around.

539
00:35:33,865 --> 00:35:35,959
- (GROANS)
- No! No!

540
00:35:38,503 --> 00:35:40,438
Stay with me, stay with me.

541
00:35:42,874 --> 00:35:44,274
(SCREAMS)

542
00:35:44,342 --> 00:35:46,038
You're never gonna
get out of here alive.

543
00:35:46,211 --> 00:35:47,543
My people are going to kill you.

544
00:35:47,646 --> 00:35:50,980
Your people? Who do you
think planted these guns?

545
00:35:51,783 --> 00:35:53,274
You can come out.

546
00:35:57,956 --> 00:35:59,049
How you doing, Doc?

547
00:35:59,157 --> 00:36:00,455
(SAMPSON LAUGHS)

548
00:36:01,626 --> 00:36:03,390
I'm having Sampson
run The Narrows.

549
00:36:03,795 --> 00:36:06,424
You should have killed me
when you had the chance.

550
00:36:06,498 --> 00:36:09,297
The fact that you didn't told
me everything I needed to know.

551
00:36:11,036 --> 00:36:12,698
(LEE GRUNTING)

552
00:36:14,472 --> 00:36:17,636
Since we're family, I'm
only going to do one hand.

553
00:36:17,709 --> 00:36:19,200
(SCREAMS VIOLENTLY)

554
00:36:33,491 --> 00:36:35,153
SOFIA: Throw her on the streets.

555
00:36:35,860 --> 00:36:36,884
(HAMMER CLATTERING)

556
00:36:36,995 --> 00:36:38,861
Let The Narrows see their queen.

557
00:36:40,331 --> 00:36:41,856
(LEE WHIMPERING)

558
00:36:50,608 --> 00:36:52,768
REPORTER: The scene here
remains largely under control,

559
00:36:52,844 --> 00:36:54,938
but Ivy Pepper remains at large.

560
00:36:55,046 --> 00:36:58,244
Now inside we have a
team of investigators...

561
00:37:00,585 --> 00:37:01,917
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

562
00:37:02,287 --> 00:37:04,119
(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)

563
00:37:07,559 --> 00:37:08,822
Yeah.

564
00:37:10,729 --> 00:37:11,856
What?

565
00:37:12,997 --> 00:37:14,226
Where is she?

566
00:37:24,776 --> 00:37:25,903
Sir?

567
00:37:26,711 --> 00:37:27,770
Sir?

568
00:37:28,213 --> 00:37:29,272
Excuse me?

569
00:37:29,748 --> 00:37:31,046
Are you family?

570
00:37:32,917 --> 00:37:34,249
I'm a cop.

571
00:37:36,421 --> 00:37:38,219
She wouldn't tell us who did it.

572
00:37:44,996 --> 00:37:46,157
She doesn't have to.

573
00:37:48,066 --> 00:37:50,160
(ALARM BUZZING)

574
00:37:55,106 --> 00:37:58,167
Arkham doesn't
get many volunteers.

575
00:37:59,410 --> 00:38:01,345
You do know who I am, right?

576
00:38:02,480 --> 00:38:04,346
Criminally insane
pretty much covers it.

577
00:38:04,749 --> 00:38:06,183
Read.

578
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:07,343
And sign.

579
00:38:07,986 --> 00:38:09,147
I'll be back.

580
00:38:16,828 --> 00:38:18,558
I hate that you
were right about this.

581
00:38:19,397 --> 00:38:20,797
But it'll keep her safe.

582
00:38:21,299 --> 00:38:22,665
Hey, Ed?

583
00:38:22,767 --> 00:38:24,258
What has two eyes but can't see?

584
00:38:24,335 --> 00:38:25,428
(SIGHS) This again.

585
00:38:26,004 --> 00:38:27,233
Two needles.

586
00:38:28,306 --> 00:38:30,275
Half of Mississippi, who cares?

587
00:38:32,610 --> 00:38:34,306
You should, Ed.

588
00:38:35,847 --> 00:38:37,008
(DOOR BUZZING AND OPENING)

589
00:38:41,186 --> 00:38:42,848
I knew you'd come.

590
00:38:44,989 --> 00:38:46,855
I knew you'd
understand my letter.

591
00:38:46,958 --> 00:38:48,153
How did you know I'd be...

592
00:38:48,893 --> 00:38:50,486
What are you talking about?

593
00:38:50,562 --> 00:38:52,463
I'm not talking to you, Ed.

594
00:38:53,898 --> 00:38:55,730
I'm talking to him.

595
00:38:55,834 --> 00:38:56,893
(LAUGHS)

596
00:38:58,837 --> 00:39:00,635
He read my letter.

597
00:39:03,474 --> 00:39:05,067
Read the first word
of each sentence.

598
00:39:07,011 --> 00:39:12,348
"Please bring Ed to
Arkham, so I can set you free."

599
00:39:12,617 --> 00:39:13,880
What has two eyes,

600
00:39:13,985 --> 00:39:16,011
but can't see what's
happening in front of him.

601
00:39:16,120 --> 00:39:18,055
- Ed Nygma!
- No.

602
00:39:19,357 --> 00:39:20,882
I came here to save Lee.

603
00:39:20,992 --> 00:39:22,824
He read my letter.

604
00:39:22,894 --> 00:39:24,021
You...

605
00:39:24,462 --> 00:39:26,124
You're wrong!

606
00:39:26,197 --> 00:39:27,688
I am Ed!

607
00:39:27,799 --> 00:39:29,665
Edward Nygma, that is it!

608
00:39:29,868 --> 00:39:32,303
Lee believes in me. She
sees me for who I am.

609
00:39:32,370 --> 00:39:34,339
But I see him,

610
00:39:34,472 --> 00:39:35,735
- Ed.
- No.

611
00:39:38,676 --> 00:39:41,168
Lee Thompkins may
have made Ed strong,

612
00:39:42,213 --> 00:39:43,772
but I see the other you.

613
00:39:48,219 --> 00:39:50,245
One whose name I wouldn't speak.

614
00:39:51,890 --> 00:39:53,688
But because he has earned it

615
00:39:53,925 --> 00:39:55,860
and because I need him,

616
00:39:56,694 --> 00:39:58,060
- I'm saying now.
- No!

617
00:39:58,129 --> 00:40:01,861
- Please, please don't.
- I need you.

618
00:40:01,933 --> 00:40:03,561
Please...

619
00:40:03,902 --> 00:40:05,029
Riddler.

620
00:40:05,103 --> 00:40:06,264
(GASPING)

621
00:40:28,359 --> 00:40:29,725
Shall we get to work?

622
00:40:33,531 --> 00:40:36,467
(BOTH LAUGHING)

623
00:40:40,972 --> 00:40:41,972
So?

624
00:40:43,408 --> 00:40:45,274
How'd you make
it off the roof then?

625
00:40:47,011 --> 00:40:48,809
A fire escape on
the next building.

626
00:40:50,014 --> 00:40:51,642
Why'd you run from Gordon?

627
00:40:52,684 --> 00:40:54,346
I mean, you could've
told him, it was you.

628
00:40:57,021 --> 00:40:58,319
I don't know.

629
00:41:01,759 --> 00:41:04,854
I just couldn't.

630
00:41:08,833 --> 00:41:10,529
I'm going to help
people, Alfred.

631
00:41:12,103 --> 00:41:16,131
And if that means accepting
every part of myself, good and bad,

632
00:41:18,009 --> 00:41:19,409
then I will.

633
00:41:23,748 --> 00:41:24,841
I do.

634
00:41:26,451 --> 00:41:27,942
It's what my parents
would've wanted.

635
00:41:29,187 --> 00:41:31,520
Your parents would've
been very proud of you.

636
00:41:35,660 --> 00:41:36,855
I'm proud of you.

637
00:41:42,834 --> 00:41:44,200
Alfred?

638
00:41:45,536 --> 00:41:46,834
If you'd

639
00:41:47,105 --> 00:41:49,301
need a ride back to
Gotham, I can drive you.

640
00:41:50,675 --> 00:41:52,371
I'm not going anywhere, sir.

641
00:41:54,746 --> 00:41:55,839
I'm home.

642
00:42:12,263 --> 00:42:13,993
Congratulations.

643
00:42:14,866 --> 00:42:16,562
I heard you saved the day.

644
00:42:17,201 --> 00:42:18,260
Good job.

645
00:42:20,238 --> 00:42:22,366
There's a reason
you're captain and I'm a

646
00:42:22,573 --> 00:42:25,407
50-year-old screwup,
pouring shots for barflies.

647
00:42:28,546 --> 00:42:31,414
There's a reason, all right,
but it's not what you think.

648
00:42:34,652 --> 00:42:36,211
I screwed up, Harv.

649
00:42:37,488 --> 00:42:38,683
I screwed up bad.

650
00:42:39,657 --> 00:42:41,457
And I'm gonna need
your help to make it right.

651
00:42:43,761 --> 00:42:45,354
Sofia hired the Pyg.

652
00:42:47,398 --> 00:42:48,593
And I knew.

653
00:42:50,802 --> 00:42:52,100
I knew...

654
00:42:53,871 --> 00:42:55,100
And I covered it up.

655
00:43:06,317 --> 00:43:08,081
And now, I'm gonna
take her down.
